5. WHAT IS NOT RESTRICTED

Nothing here is intended to restrict:

  (a) the playing of the game;
  (b) the description, explanation, review or teaching of how it is played;
  (c) the independent creation of a different work that happens to employ
      comparable game mechanics, mechanics as such not being the subject of
      copyright protection; or
  (d) any act permitted by applicable law notwithstanding this notice,
      including quotation, parody, private copying and the exceptions provided
      for the interoperability and study of computer programs.

The rightholder reserves, separately from copyright, any action available under
the law of unfair competition in respect of imitation that entails an undue
